WEBVTT

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.501
Report.

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.407
A ship just de-cloaked
off our port stern.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.775
Can you identify them?

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:14.279
They re-cloaked.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.939
That disruptor blast

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.245
had a Klingon signature.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:20.944
Evasive maneuvers.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:22.112
Hail them.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.747
No response.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.926
Port shields
are down to 50 percent.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.065
They've re-cloaked again.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.899
The tetryon readings indicate

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.598
it's a D7-class cruiser.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:43.472
D7? They were
retired decades ago.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.477
If their technology
is antiquated...

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:46.637
Perhaps a metaphasic

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.577
scan might be able

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.547
to penetrate their cloak.

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:50.583
Do it.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.515
Bridge to Astrometrics.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.053
Initiate a metaphasic sweep.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.984
I've detected a vessel.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.923
Transferring the trajectory
to Tactical.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.586
I have them.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.460
Fire phasers.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.100
Our cloak has failed.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:16.939
Divert emergency power
to shields.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.240
Forward emitters are off-line.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:22.372
The Federation ship
is hailing again.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.643
Answer them.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.944
Captain!

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.245
It may give us more time

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.219
to get the cloak
back on line. Visual.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.524
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:33.616
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:34.785
Stand down.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.056
We will not surrender
to sworn enemies

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.495
of the Klingon Empire.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.937
I think there's been
a misunderstanding.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.875
The Empire signed
a peace treaty

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:36.211
with the Federation
more than 80 years ago.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.579
If I'm not mistaken,

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.947
it's still in effect.

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:40.076
You're lying.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:43.645
I'm not lying,
but even if I were,

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.657
your ship is no match for mine.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:47.955
I suggest we discuss this.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.517
What is there to talk about?

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.928
The treaty, for one thing.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.465
I'll give you access
to our database,

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.262
show you I'm
telling the truth.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.929
Databases can be falsified.

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:02.065
I have a Klingon serving
aboard this ship.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.472
Impossible.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.101
She's my Chief Engineer.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:09.274
I will meet this Chief Engineer.

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:12.216
We'd be honored
to have you as our guest.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:19.190
You're safe here;
you have my word.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.886
Forgive me
if I don't find the word

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.257
of a human very reassuring.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.852
I'd like to know
what you're doing

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:24.919
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:26.556
I'm not answering
any questions

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:27.998
until I see the Klingon.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.910
Captain Kohlar,
Lieutenant Torres,

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.075
our Chief Engineer.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:48.917
You're with child.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:51.252
That's what
the Doctor tells me.

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:54.691
Did you conceive during
the holy month of nay'Poq?

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:56.854
I have no idea.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.261
It would have been
14 or 15 weeks ago.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:00.890
That sounds about right,

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.435
not that it's any
of your business.

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:06.904
I must return to my ship.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:09.203
Aren't you interested
in learning about the treaty?

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:11.243
Here's a copy
of the Khitomer Accords.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.778
I must return to my vessel.

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.244
Not without your assurance

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.373
that you won't fire
on my ship again.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.781
You have my word.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:30.791
Escort Captain Kohlar
back to the Transporter Room.

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.524
Aye, Captain.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:44.107
What the hell was that about?

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:46.944
It's the truth.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.514
How can you be certain?

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:50.514
The Scrolls say:

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:53.211
"You will find me
after two warring houses

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:54.947
make peace."

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.353
Our people and the Federation,

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:01.018
our greatest enemy,
are at peace.

00:06:01.094 --> 00:06:03.892
So the humans claim.

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:06.625
These Accords may be
a deception.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:08.360
The other signs are present.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:12.598
"You will know me
before I know the world."

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.731
The child is unborn.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:16.832
It does not know the world.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:19.207
You interpret the Scrolls well.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:21.906
We must verify the evidence.

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:24.312
Your skepticism darkens
my heart, T'Greth.

00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:26.477
What evidence did
our ancestors have

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.679
when they began this journey?

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:31.349
Nothing but their faith.

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:34.450
Tell the others to prepare.

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:38.520
The Day of Separation
has arrived.

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:50.905
Captain, the Klingon ship...
its core is breaching.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.410
Red Alert.

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.503
Hail them.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.639
I salute you, Captain.

00:06:56.716 --> 00:07:00.709
You did more damage to our
vessel than my engineer thought.

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:01.879
We can send over a team

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:04.148
to help you establish
a containment field.

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.986
- There isn't time.
- He's right.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:08.390
Their core is going to breach
in less than 30 seconds.

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.520
I'm requesting
emergency transport.

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:11.893
Captain...

00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:14.262
their crew complement is 204.

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:20.738
Erect force fields
around the Shuttle Bay.

00:07:20.807 --> 00:07:22.035
Transport them there.

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:24.576
Tell your crew to stand by
for evacuation.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:25.576
Ten seconds.

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:26.669
If we're still too close

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:28.077
when their core breaches...

00:07:28.147 --> 00:07:29.978
Go to warp as soon as their crew
is aboard.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.248
Five...

00:07:32.318 --> 00:07:34.616
four, three...

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:36.416
We have them.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:56.401
You spared us
a dishonorable death.

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:57.943
Sensor logs indicate

00:07:58.044 --> 00:08:01.411
that the containment failure
was not caused by our weapons.

00:08:01.481 --> 00:08:03.642
You activated
a self-destruct sequence.

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:06.276
It was the only way
to get us aboard Voyager.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:07.979
Why was that so important?

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:10.113
It's our sacred duty

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:12.054
to be here.

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.887
I don't understand.

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:16.790
More than 100 years ago,

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:20.526
my great-grandfather
was part of a sect

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.569
which believed
the Empire had lost its way.

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:26.400
They discovered a sacred text.

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.372
It told them to embark
on a journey

00:08:28.441 --> 00:08:30.306
to a distant region
of the galaxy.

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:34.779
You've been traveling
for four generations?

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:36.712
My people have always known

00:08:36.782 --> 00:08:39.683
the voyage would be long
and difficult,

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:42.414
but the Scrolls said
we would be rewarded.

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.346
How?

00:08:45.424 --> 00:08:48.655
We would find the kuvah'magh,

00:08:48.728 --> 00:08:50.696
the savior of our people,

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:54.392
the one who will lead us
to a new Empire.

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:55.832
The Scrolls instruct us

00:08:55.902 --> 00:08:57.733
to follow her
wherever she goes.

00:08:57.803 --> 00:09:00.499
What does any of this have to do
with Voyager?

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:07.877
I believe the kuvah'magh is the
unborn child of B'Elanna Torres.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.413
You're joking.

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:13.179
They take their beliefs
very seriously.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:16.050
Seriously enough to destroy
their own ship?

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:18.113
Couldn't they have
just followed us?

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.887
Apparently, their sacred text
told them to cast off

00:09:22.028 --> 00:09:25.828
the old ways as soon as
they found this kuvah'magh.

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.126
They saw their vessel

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:29.690
as the last vestige
of the corrupt Empire.

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:31.566
I was hoping our daughter
would be special,

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:32.569
but I never dreamed

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:34.299
she'd turn out to be
the Klingon messiah.

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:35.465
This isn't funny.

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:36.633
They might be dangerous.

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:38.904
I mean, and what if they want
to hurt the baby?

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:40.342
To them, your baby's sacred.

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:42.745
It's unlikely they would do
anything to harm her.

00:09:42.815 --> 00:09:43.747
200 Klingons pose

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:45.044
a significant
security threat.

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:46.277
I suggest we keep
them confined

00:09:46.352 --> 00:09:47.319
to the Shuttle Bay

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:49.047
until we can find a
suitable home for them.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:50.918
There are women and children
down there.

00:09:51.057 --> 00:09:52.354
We can't just lock them up.

00:09:52.425 --> 00:09:53.357
I agree.

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:54.358
Captain...

00:09:54.427 --> 00:09:55.917
Assign extra security
to every deck,

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:58.553
and make sure the Klingons know
and abide by the rules.

00:09:58.631 --> 00:10:00.861
The Bridge will have
to be off limits.

00:10:00.933 --> 00:10:02.127
Engineering as well.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.930
Keep them out
of all restricted areas.

00:10:04.036 --> 00:10:06.266
Despite their reverence
for Lieutenant Torres,

00:10:06.339 --> 00:10:08.807
she should be assigned
a 24-hour security detail.

00:10:08.874 --> 00:10:10.501
Just what I need.

00:10:10.576 --> 00:10:12.203
Where are they
going to sleep?

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:14.109
We'll double up in quarters.

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:15.738
I'll ask for volunteers.

00:10:15.815 --> 00:10:17.578
I know this isn't going
to be easy,

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.948
but until we can find
another place for them,

00:10:20.052 --> 00:10:22.850
we should do our best
to make them feel comfortable.

00:10:22.922 --> 00:10:24.116
Dismissed.

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:44.075
Captain, you must try the gagh.

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:46.407
I'll pass, thank you,
but I'm glad to see

00:10:46.479 --> 00:10:48.777
you're getting into
the spirit of things.

00:10:48.848 --> 00:10:51.214
Well, I've been studying
the Klingon database.

00:10:51.283 --> 00:10:54.081
They're a fascinating
people; very robust,

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:56.747
and, uh, they certainly
seem to appreciate

00:10:56.822 --> 00:10:58.983
my culinary skills.

00:10:59.058 --> 00:11:00.923
It looks like everything's
running smoothly.

00:11:00.993 --> 00:11:03.427
Uh, not quite everything.

00:11:03.496 --> 00:11:05.691
Some of the Starfleet people

00:11:05.765 --> 00:11:07.630
have been complaining...

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.565
about the smell.

00:11:09.635 --> 00:11:12.331
Personally, I
find it appealing.

00:11:12.405 --> 00:11:15.272
A kind of musky aroma.

00:11:15.341 --> 00:11:17.332
Maybe we can adjust
the environmental controls

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:19.674
to filter out the musk.

00:11:19.745 --> 00:11:21.440
Thief!

00:11:21.514 --> 00:11:24.449
Touch my food again,
and I'll kill you!

00:11:24.517 --> 00:11:25.950
Okay, everybody relax.

00:11:26.018 --> 00:11:27.918
He took gagh from my plate.

00:11:27.987 --> 00:11:29.579
If you don't mind, Ensign,

00:11:29.655 --> 00:11:31.782
I've been studying
Klingon etiquette.

00:11:31.857 --> 00:11:33.722
You shouldn't quarrel
over food.

00:11:33.793 --> 00:11:35.761
Save your strength for battle,

00:11:35.828 --> 00:11:38.262
to fight those
who would challenge you.

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:40.560
Take it easy!

00:11:42.601 --> 00:11:43.966
That's enough!

00:11:44.036 --> 00:11:46.869
You have a fiery spirit.

00:11:48.574 --> 00:11:50.701
You will make a worthy mate.

00:11:53.412 --> 00:11:54.879
What a day!

00:11:59.852 --> 00:12:03.788
I never met a more
ravenous group in my life.

00:12:03.856 --> 00:12:07.189
I must have served
over 300 meals.

00:12:07.259 --> 00:12:11.286
Mr. Neelix, may I ask
what you're doing here?

00:12:11.363 --> 00:12:13.695
We're bunkmates.

00:12:13.766 --> 00:12:17.202
There must be some mistake.

00:12:17.269 --> 00:12:19.635
No, there's no mistake.

00:12:19.705 --> 00:12:21.832
I gave up my quarters
to a Klingon family.

00:12:21.907 --> 00:12:24.239
By the time I checked
with Commander Chakotay,

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:26.801
you were the only one
who hadn't been paired up.

00:12:26.879 --> 00:12:28.744
You should've consulted me.

00:12:28.814 --> 00:12:33.308
We're such close friends,
I knew you wouldn't mind.

00:12:33.385 --> 00:12:37.378
Mr. Neelix, as much
as I enjoy your company,

00:12:37.456 --> 00:12:40.892
I prefer solitude
in my own quarters.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:43.428
You don't really want me
to go back there

00:12:43.496 --> 00:12:45.987
and tell that family
to get out, do you?

00:12:48.267 --> 00:12:50.963
Good, because I promise you

00:12:51.036 --> 00:12:54.631
we're going to have fun,
Mr. Vulcan.

00:12:56.175 --> 00:13:00.043
I learned
some Klingon drinking songs.

00:13:02.248 --> 00:13:03.772
I'll teach them to you.

00:13:03.849 --> 00:13:06.443
Ej IM-ta fey DE-ja i

00:13:06.519 --> 00:13:10.751
ejdahk-so-TAS
ghos va Skral byteek

00:13:10.823 --> 00:13:13.587
Ej IM-ta fey DE-ja i...

00:13:13.659 --> 00:13:15.126
Paris to Torres.

00:13:15.194 --> 00:13:16.786
I'm almost finished.

00:13:16.862 --> 00:13:18.454
You said that an hour ago.

00:13:18.531 --> 00:13:20.795
I'll be there in a minute,
I promise. Torres out.

00:13:20.866 --> 00:13:22.800
Keep an eye on the replicators.

00:13:22.868 --> 00:13:24.699
They've already gone down
once today.

00:13:25.771 --> 00:13:27.363
It's her!

00:13:39.151 --> 00:13:41.312
When you said,
"Be there in a minute,"

00:13:41.387 --> 00:13:42.945
you weren't kidding.

00:13:43.055 --> 00:13:46.388
A group of Klingons ambushed me
outside of Engineering.

00:13:46.458 --> 00:13:48.653
I decided transporting myself

00:13:48.727 --> 00:13:51.491
would be easier
than running the gauntlet.

00:13:51.564 --> 00:13:53.964
I'm starting to feel
like a prisoner.

00:13:54.033 --> 00:13:57.469
Well, at least you have
a handsome cell mate.

00:13:57.536 --> 00:14:00.096
How long do you think
they're going to be on board?

00:14:00.172 --> 00:14:03.403
I thought you'd be glad
to have other Klingons around.

00:14:03.475 --> 00:14:04.737
You've always told me

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:07.438
how uncomfortable it
is being the only one.

00:14:07.513 --> 00:14:09.811
I guess I should be
careful what I wish for.

00:14:09.882 --> 00:14:11.645
Maybe you should
talk to some of them...

00:14:11.717 --> 00:14:12.809
give them a chance.

00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:14.820
Come in.

00:14:16.055 --> 00:14:18.455
Captain...

00:14:18.524 --> 00:14:20.321
I'm sorry to bother you,
but I need your help.

00:14:20.392 --> 00:14:22.360
Ten of the Klingons
have started a hunger strike.

00:14:22.428 --> 00:14:24.089
They say they won't eat
until you agree

00:14:24.163 --> 00:14:25.790
to meet with their
Council of Elders.

00:14:25.865 --> 00:14:27.298
That's ridiculous.

00:14:27.366 --> 00:14:29.926
Their faith is obviously
very important to them.

00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:32.026
They think I'm
something I'm not.

00:14:32.104 --> 00:14:34.800
Just talk to them;
hear what they have to say.

00:14:35.875 --> 00:14:38.571
We could be with
these people for a while.

00:14:38.644 --> 00:14:40.305
You can't avoid them forever.

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:41.607
I can try.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:43.580
If it'll make you
feel any better,

00:14:43.649 --> 00:14:45.844
I'll go with you.

00:14:48.787 --> 00:14:51.813
MobaR, DoH'lo maj, Qo-vuh'makh.

00:14:51.891 --> 00:14:54.951
MobaR, DoH'lo maj,
Qo-vuh'makh.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:58.223
MobaR, DoH'lo maj, Qo-vuh'makh.

00:14:58.297 --> 00:15:01.391
MobaR, DoH'lo maj,
Qo-vuh'makh.

00:15:01.467 --> 00:15:04.732
MobaR, DoH'lo maj, Qo-vuh'makh.

00:15:04.803 --> 00:15:07.897
MobaR, DoH'lo maj,
Qo-vuh'makh.

00:15:08.007 --> 00:15:10.737
MobaR, DoH'lo maj, Qo-vuh'makh.

00:15:10.809 --> 00:15:12.106
MobaR...

00:15:13.679 --> 00:15:15.840
You honor us
with your presence.

00:15:17.549 --> 00:15:20.450
Look at her ridges.

00:15:20.519 --> 00:15:22.714
Morak was right.

00:15:22.788 --> 00:15:25.621
Your blood is not pure.

00:15:25.691 --> 00:15:30.060
No. My father was human.

00:15:32.031 --> 00:15:34.124
Couldn't you see this
for yourself?

00:15:34.199 --> 00:15:35.530
Yes, but...

00:15:35.601 --> 00:15:36.932
Why didn't you tell us?!

00:15:37.002 --> 00:15:38.094
It wasn't important!

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:41.628
Not important?

00:15:41.707 --> 00:15:43.368
We destroyed our ship

00:15:43.442 --> 00:15:46.240
because you said
she was the mother

00:15:46.312 --> 00:15:47.540
of the kuvah'magh.

00:15:47.613 --> 00:15:49.478
Show me where it's written

00:15:49.548 --> 00:15:52.608
that the kuvah'magh
must have pure Klingon blood.

00:15:52.685 --> 00:15:55.586
The prophecy wouldn't lead us
to a mongrel child.

00:15:55.654 --> 00:15:58.418
Hey, take it easy.

00:15:58.490 --> 00:15:59.787
Who are you?

00:15:59.858 --> 00:16:02.884
The father
of that mongrel child.

00:16:03.028 --> 00:16:04.996
More human blood.

00:16:05.064 --> 00:16:08.591
Your kuvah'magh
isn't even half Klingon.

00:16:08.667 --> 00:16:10.726
I've spent my life

00:16:10.803 --> 00:16:12.532
interpreting the Scrolls,

00:16:12.604 --> 00:16:15.767
and I say that all the signs
of the prophecy are here.

00:16:15.841 --> 00:16:17.775
Liar.

00:16:17.843 --> 00:16:22.041
You've led us to a false savior.

00:16:31.357 --> 00:16:33.120
I told you this
was a mistake.

00:16:33.192 --> 00:16:36.059
Lieutenant...
I need your help.

00:16:36.128 --> 00:16:37.060
Any more "help"

00:16:37.129 --> 00:16:38.061
from me, and you're going

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:39.392
to have a holy war
on your hands.

00:16:39.465 --> 00:16:41.729
That's what
I'm trying to prevent.

00:16:48.574 --> 00:16:51.600
My baby's just a baby.

00:16:51.677 --> 00:16:52.905
She's not a savior.

00:16:52.978 --> 00:16:53.945
Perhaps you're right,

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:57.139
but we must convince
my people that she is.

00:16:57.216 --> 00:16:59.047
Why?

00:16:59.118 --> 00:17:01.609
We've traveled more
than 30,000 light-years

00:17:01.687 --> 00:17:03.882
in search of this savior,

00:17:03.989 --> 00:17:08.449
and in more than 100 years,
we've found nothing

00:17:08.527 --> 00:17:11.496
except hardship and isolation.

00:17:11.563 --> 00:17:14.225
When I saw Lieutenant Torres...

00:17:14.299 --> 00:17:16.494
that she was with child...

00:17:16.568 --> 00:17:18.502
I didn't know if I was looking

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:21.038
at the mother
of the kuvah'magh or not,

00:17:21.106 --> 00:17:23.597
but I did know I was
looking at an opportunity

00:17:23.675 --> 00:17:25.370
to end this wasteful journey.

00:17:25.444 --> 00:17:27.844
Then you don't believe
in the prophecy?

00:17:27.913 --> 00:17:29.107
What I believe

00:17:29.181 --> 00:17:31.342
is that my people
have suffered enough.

00:17:31.417 --> 00:17:34.079
If they accept your child
as the kuvah'magh,

00:17:34.153 --> 00:17:36.553
you'll hold
great influence over them.

00:17:36.622 --> 00:17:38.783
We can find a suitable planet.

00:17:38.857 --> 00:17:40.722
You can tell them
it's their new home,

00:17:40.793 --> 00:17:42.283
and they'll follow you there.

00:17:42.361 --> 00:17:44.761
I'm not going to lie to them.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:46.661
What's the alternative?

00:17:46.732 --> 00:17:49.132
My people
staying aboard your ship,

00:17:49.201 --> 00:17:50.793
draining your resources?

00:17:50.869 --> 00:17:52.393
I agree with
Lieutenant Torres.

00:17:52.471 --> 00:17:54.939
I'm not comfortable
deceiving your people.

00:17:55.007 --> 00:17:57.532
Perhaps you won't have to lie
to them to convince them.

00:17:57.609 --> 00:17:59.600
What are you suggesting?

00:17:59.678 --> 00:18:02.545
If you
study the Scrolls with me,

00:18:02.614 --> 00:18:04.582
we may be able to interpret them

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:07.744
in a way that appears consistent
with the events of your life.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.811
Then we'll bring
those consistencies

00:18:09.888 --> 00:18:12.254
to the attention
of the Council.

00:18:12.324 --> 00:18:14.884
So... you just

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.894
want to stretch
the truth a little?

00:18:16.995 --> 00:18:20.055
It is possible
that the Sacred Scrolls

00:18:20.132 --> 00:18:22.862
were scrawled
by a madman in a cave,

00:18:22.935 --> 00:18:25.904
or perhaps they really were
divinely inspired.

00:18:26.004 --> 00:18:27.904
Either way, they've guided us

00:18:28.006 --> 00:18:29.564
for over a century.

00:18:29.641 --> 00:18:30.733
If my people

00:18:30.809 --> 00:18:33.437
start to believe
that the Sacred Scrolls

00:18:33.512 --> 00:18:37.312
have led them astray,
there may be violence.

00:18:37.382 --> 00:18:39.475
Is that a threat?

00:18:39.551 --> 00:18:41.485
Merely a fact.

00:18:41.553 --> 00:18:44.317
You're doing
everything you can

00:18:44.389 --> 00:18:46.516
to get your people home,
Captain.

00:18:46.592 --> 00:18:49.789
That's all I'm doing for mine.

00:18:53.332 --> 00:18:56.028
It says, "The kuvah'magh

00:18:56.101 --> 00:19:00.197
will be descended
from a noble house."

00:19:00.272 --> 00:19:02.331
I don't come from one,

00:19:02.407 --> 00:19:04.773
and I'm pretty sure
my husband doesn't either.

00:19:04.843 --> 00:19:07.107
We all have nobility
in our blood,

00:19:07.179 --> 00:19:09.010
if we go back far enough.

00:19:09.081 --> 00:19:12.175
So these Scrolls can mean
anything you want them to.

00:19:12.251 --> 00:19:16.017
It is written that the mother
of the kuvah'magh

00:19:16.088 --> 00:19:18.079
would be an off-worlder.

00:19:18.157 --> 00:19:20.318
Weren't you born

00:19:20.392 --> 00:19:21.381
on a Federation colony?

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.485
A lot of Klingons
are born off-world.

00:19:23.562 --> 00:19:26.725
It also says that you would've
lived a life of solitude

00:19:26.798 --> 00:19:29.358
and endured many hardships.

00:19:29.434 --> 00:19:31.163
That's accurate, isn't it?

00:19:32.971 --> 00:19:36.839
According to this,
I'm supposed to have won

00:19:36.909 --> 00:19:39.742
"a glorious victory against
an army of 10,000 warriors."

00:19:39.811 --> 00:19:41.711
Haven't you?

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:45.511
We haven't even encountered
10,000 warriors...

00:19:45.584 --> 00:19:47.552
well, unless
you include the Borg.

00:19:47.619 --> 00:19:51.487
Did you help destroy
one of their vessels?

00:19:51.557 --> 00:19:52.615
I suppose...

00:19:52.691 --> 00:19:56.127
Couldn't that have been
your glorious victory?

00:19:56.195 --> 00:19:59.028
I guess so.

00:19:59.097 --> 00:20:01.497
Where are the images of Kahless?

00:20:01.567 --> 00:20:03.933
Where is your family crest?

00:20:04.002 --> 00:20:07.597
They clashed with the carpet.

00:20:07.673 --> 00:20:12.269
Don't you honor any
of your people's traditions?

00:20:12.344 --> 00:20:14.904
Not really.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:18.006
There is one tradition
we can honor together.

00:20:21.954 --> 00:20:23.444
What are you doing?

00:20:23.522 --> 00:20:26.116
It's midday.

00:20:26.191 --> 00:20:29.627
Time to remember the sacrifice
of our ancestors.

00:20:31.363 --> 00:20:33.354
Haven't you made
a Plea for the Dead before?

00:20:33.432 --> 00:20:35.400
Well, not since I was a child.

00:20:35.467 --> 00:20:38.493
The dead can't rest
in Sto-Vo-Kor

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:41.130
if the living
don't honor their memory.

00:20:44.042 --> 00:20:47.944
Perhaps there's someone
I can honor on your behalf.

00:20:48.013 --> 00:20:51.107
Who did you plead
for as a child?

00:20:51.183 --> 00:20:52.980
My grandmother.

00:20:53.118 --> 00:20:54.983
She was called?

00:20:55.087 --> 00:20:56.384
L'Naan.

00:21:00.826 --> 00:21:03.158
Kahless...

00:21:03.228 --> 00:21:07.289
we implore you to
remember those warriors

00:21:07.366 --> 00:21:10.563
who have fallen
in your name.

00:21:10.636 --> 00:21:15.130
Lift them out of
the cavern of despair

00:21:15.207 --> 00:21:19.337
and reveal yourself to them

00:21:19.411 --> 00:21:20.537
in all your glory.

00:21:20.612 --> 00:21:22.944
Right, "in all your glory."

00:21:23.081 --> 00:21:28.041
Remember Kolax, son of Amar.

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:30.782
Remember Talij,

00:21:30.856 --> 00:21:34.417
daughter of K'Rene.

00:21:37.029 --> 00:21:40.123
Remember L'Naan,

00:21:40.198 --> 00:21:42.132
daughter of Krelik.

00:21:57.582 --> 00:21:59.174
What happened to you?

00:21:59.251 --> 00:22:00.878
I cut myself shaving.

00:22:00.952 --> 00:22:02.886
Is that a bite mark?

00:22:02.954 --> 00:22:04.785
One of the Klingons attacked me.

00:22:04.856 --> 00:22:06.653
Did you do something
to provoke him?

00:22:06.725 --> 00:22:08.784
Not him, her,

00:22:08.860 --> 00:22:11.829
and she wasn't provoked,
she was... aroused.

00:22:11.897 --> 00:22:12.921
Ah...

00:22:13.031 --> 00:22:14.760
I'm not surprised.

00:22:14.833 --> 00:22:16.926
I've studied the section
on Klingon mating rituals

00:22:17.035 --> 00:22:18.764
in their cultural database.

00:22:18.837 --> 00:22:19.861
Then maybe you can

00:22:19.938 --> 00:22:21.929
tell me how to convince
a female twice my size

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:23.735
that I'm not interested.

00:22:23.809 --> 00:22:25.367
Hmm, you probably can't.

00:22:25.444 --> 00:22:26.502
Great.

00:22:26.578 --> 00:22:29.877
As I understand it,
you have two options...

00:22:29.948 --> 00:22:33.281
kill her or mate with her.

00:22:33.352 --> 00:22:36.219
Since the first option
is clearly unacceptable...

00:22:36.288 --> 00:22:37.380
What's this?

00:22:37.456 --> 00:22:39.617
Authorization for you to engage
in intimate relations

00:22:39.691 --> 00:22:41.158
with a member
of an alien species.

00:22:41.226 --> 00:22:44.491
Be sure to get the Captain's
approval as well.

00:22:44.563 --> 00:22:49.227
Chief Engineer's Personal Log,
Stardate 54518.2.

00:22:49.301 --> 00:22:52.464
I've spent the last two days
reviewing the Sacred Scrolls

00:22:52.537 --> 00:22:54.596
in preparation
for my appearance

00:22:54.673 --> 00:22:56.265
before the Klingon Council.

00:22:56.341 --> 00:22:59.572
Kohlar also suggested I prepare
a few "colorful stories"

00:22:59.644 --> 00:23:01.077
to help win them over.

00:23:01.146 --> 00:23:02.875
That's when they
beamed aboard the Flyer,

00:23:02.948 --> 00:23:04.677
weapons firing.

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:06.513
Tuvok and Neelix
fought valiantly,

00:23:06.585 --> 00:23:08.212
but there were too many Hirogen.

00:23:08.286 --> 00:23:14.384
I had to face ten
of their fiercest hunters alone.

00:23:14.459 --> 00:23:17.223
Is that how you remember it?

00:23:17.295 --> 00:23:20.731
Exaggeration is part
of Klingon custom.

00:23:20.799 --> 00:23:21.891
She's doing great.

00:23:21.967 --> 00:23:24.367
...were shot out of my hand,
forcing me to take down

00:23:24.436 --> 00:23:27.633
the last hunter
in hand-to-hand combat.

00:23:27.706 --> 00:23:29.799
It was a glorious fight.

00:23:29.875 --> 00:23:33.504
Your ancestors would be honored.

00:23:38.717 --> 00:23:42.118
You tell a good story,

00:23:42.187 --> 00:23:44.781
but that's not why you're here.

00:23:44.856 --> 00:23:49.452
Some say you are the mother
of the kuvah'magh,

00:23:49.528 --> 00:23:50.927
the one who will guide us

00:23:50.996 --> 00:23:52.861
to a new homeworld.

00:23:52.931 --> 00:23:56.799
Has your unborn child
told you where it is?

00:24:00.839 --> 00:24:02.898
The Scrolls say,

00:24:02.974 --> 00:24:09.470
"You will follow in my footsteps
before I have made them."

00:24:11.583 --> 00:24:13.813
Yesterday, we changed course

00:24:13.885 --> 00:24:18.254
toward a planet
very much like Qo'noS.

00:24:18.323 --> 00:24:20.814
So, in a manner of speaking,

00:24:20.892 --> 00:24:24.851
you are now following
my child to a new home.

00:24:26.531 --> 00:24:29.125
You deliver the words
we want to hear,

00:24:29.201 --> 00:24:31.135
but it's Kohlar
who gives them to you.

00:24:32.871 --> 00:24:35.271
Are you his puppet
in the bedchamber as well?

00:24:35.340 --> 00:24:36.637
Watch it.

00:24:36.708 --> 00:24:38.505
That's my wife
you're talking about.

00:24:38.577 --> 00:24:40.340
He speaks!

00:24:40.412 --> 00:24:41.879
I didn't think you had a tongue.

00:24:41.947 --> 00:24:43.539
Leave him out of this.

00:24:43.615 --> 00:24:45.845
You see how he hides

00:24:45.917 --> 00:24:48.215
behind his female?

00:24:48.286 --> 00:24:50.652
It is also written
that the father

00:24:50.722 --> 00:24:55.125
of the kuvah'magh will be
an honorable warrior.

00:24:55.193 --> 00:24:58.856
Would an honorable warrior
ever refuse a challenge?

00:24:58.930 --> 00:25:01.694
I haven't refused any challenge.

00:25:01.766 --> 00:25:05.327
I haven't made one yet.

00:25:09.608 --> 00:25:11.701
You and I...

00:25:13.912 --> 00:25:16.142
to the death.

00:25:16.214 --> 00:25:18.444
Tom...

00:25:18.517 --> 00:25:19.882
Stay out of this.

00:25:21.820 --> 00:25:23.447
Pahtk.

00:25:29.961 --> 00:25:31.622
I accept.

00:25:42.440 --> 00:25:44.101
What was I supposed to say?

00:25:44.175 --> 00:25:45.540
How about "no"?

00:25:45.610 --> 00:25:46.736
Th-they were all watching.

00:25:46.811 --> 00:25:48.244
There would have been
a riot if I refused.

00:25:48.313 --> 00:25:49.678
So, you're going to
get yourself killed?

00:25:49.748 --> 00:25:51.943
What makes you
so sure I'd lose?

00:25:52.017 --> 00:25:53.211
Oh, please.

00:25:53.285 --> 00:25:54.513
Look, I have no intention

00:25:54.586 --> 00:25:56.213
of fighting anyone to the death,

00:25:56.288 --> 00:25:57.915
but wasn't the
whole point of this

00:25:57.989 --> 00:25:58.956
to get them to believe

00:25:59.057 --> 00:26:00.615
that we are the parents
of their savior?

00:26:00.692 --> 00:26:01.659
Captain, this has
gone too far.

00:26:01.726 --> 00:26:02.715
You've got to
put a stop to it.

00:26:02.794 --> 00:26:04.989
I intend to.

00:26:05.063 --> 00:26:06.553
Mr. Tuvok.

00:26:11.469 --> 00:26:13.994
Gentlemen...

00:26:14.072 --> 00:26:15.198
I'm afraid Lieutenant Paris

00:26:15.273 --> 00:26:17.207
had no authority
to accept this challenge.

00:26:17.275 --> 00:26:19.743
There will be no death
matches aboard my ship.

00:26:19.811 --> 00:26:23.212
I told you this pahtk
was not the true father.

00:26:23.281 --> 00:26:25.044
Lieutenant Paris
is perfectly willing

00:26:25.116 --> 00:26:26.344
to fight you, Mr. T'Greth.

00:26:26.418 --> 00:26:28.909
I'm the one preventing him
from doing so.

00:26:28.987 --> 00:26:31.615
The father
of the kuvah'magh

00:26:31.690 --> 00:26:34.158
wouldn't let a woman
speak for him.

00:26:34.225 --> 00:26:36.716
T'Greth...

00:26:36.795 --> 00:26:39.696
there is precedent
for an honorable compromise.

00:26:41.499 --> 00:26:42.864
A nonlethal bout,

00:26:42.934 --> 00:26:44.902
fought with
blunted bat'leths.

00:26:44.970 --> 00:26:46.835
The victory goes
to the first warrior

00:26:46.905 --> 00:26:49.465
to knock his opponent
to the ground three times.

00:26:49.541 --> 00:26:50.599
A coward's rules!

00:26:50.675 --> 00:26:52.267
Was the Emperor Mur'Eq
a coward?

00:26:53.812 --> 00:26:55.746
He was the one
who instituted these rules

00:26:55.814 --> 00:26:58.305
to insure that his warriors
would kill their enemies

00:26:58.383 --> 00:26:59.611
and not each other.

00:27:01.353 --> 00:27:04.015
If you agree to these terms...

00:27:04.089 --> 00:27:05.317
I'll allow the match.

00:27:07.125 --> 00:27:10.117
I'll see you on the field

00:27:10.195 --> 00:27:11.389
of battle!

00:27:15.934 --> 00:27:18.835
I assume you have a suitable
holodeck training program

00:27:18.903 --> 00:27:21.167
for this, Lieutenant?

00:27:21.239 --> 00:27:22.672
He'll be ready.

00:27:22.741 --> 00:27:24.675
I'll train him myself.

00:27:32.050 --> 00:27:35.383
Hi.

00:27:35.453 --> 00:27:37.751
Psst! Neelix.

00:27:39.457 --> 00:27:40.389
Something wrong, Harry?

00:27:40.458 --> 00:27:41.390
Shh!

00:27:41.459 --> 00:27:42.391
Have you seen her?

00:27:42.460 --> 00:27:43.392
Who?

00:27:43.461 --> 00:27:45.486
Uh... that Klingon woman.

00:27:45.563 --> 00:27:47.929
The one I got into
a scrape with in the Mess Hall.

00:27:48.066 --> 00:27:49.465
Officer Ch'Rega.

00:27:49.534 --> 00:27:50.933
That's her.

00:27:51.036 --> 00:27:52.162
I haven't seen her today.

00:27:52.237 --> 00:27:54.467
She's been following
me everywhere.

00:27:54.539 --> 00:27:55.471
Why?

00:27:55.540 --> 00:27:56.598
She wants to mate.

00:27:56.675 --> 00:27:58.643
Oh!

00:27:58.710 --> 00:28:00.200
You're a lucky man.

00:28:00.278 --> 00:28:02.644
She's a fine specimen
of Klingon womanhood.

00:28:02.714 --> 00:28:05.114
I guess it's
a matter of taste.

00:28:05.183 --> 00:28:06.150
You never saw me!

00:28:06.217 --> 00:28:08.117
Wait!

00:28:08.186 --> 00:28:09.118
I have a better idea.

00:28:09.187 --> 00:28:11.121
Neelix, what the hell
are you doing?

00:28:11.189 --> 00:28:12.121
Play along.

00:28:12.190 --> 00:28:13.782
I'm taking her off your hands.

00:28:13.858 --> 00:28:15.382
When I say you're limited

00:28:15.460 --> 00:28:18.361
to two servings of brak't,
that's all you get!

00:28:18.430 --> 00:28:19.795
Do you understand me, Ensign?

00:28:19.864 --> 00:28:21.991
Yes, sir, whatever you say.

00:28:22.067 --> 00:28:23.329
I don't think you do.

00:28:23.401 --> 00:28:24.891
If I catch you
eating more than

00:28:24.969 --> 00:28:25.901
your share again,

00:28:25.970 --> 00:28:27.995
I'll cut it out of your belly.

00:28:29.374 --> 00:28:30.068
Run.

00:28:31.509 --> 00:28:32.498
Excuse me.

00:28:32.577 --> 00:28:35.045
Pahtk.

00:28:52.363 --> 00:28:53.694
I didn't think you approved

00:28:53.765 --> 00:28:55.164
of this kind of competition.

00:28:55.233 --> 00:28:58.725
I don't. I'm here
in an official capacity.

00:28:58.803 --> 00:28:59.929
Well, you do know
they're fighting

00:29:00.038 --> 00:29:00.970
with nonlethal weapons?

00:29:01.039 --> 00:29:03.303
You'd be surprised
how much damage

00:29:03.374 --> 00:29:04.898
a blunt bat'leth can do.

00:29:06.511 --> 00:29:08.103
Warriors, assemble!

00:29:11.015 --> 00:29:14.075
Today would be a
very bad day to die.

00:29:14.152 --> 00:29:15.278
I'll try to remember that.

00:29:18.790 --> 00:29:22.282
Let honor guide you!

00:29:22.360 --> 00:29:24.157
Tagh!

00:29:29.167 --> 00:29:32.625
I see fear in your eyes, human.

00:29:32.704 --> 00:29:34.695
The only Klingon I'm afraid of

00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:36.832
is my wife after she's worked
a double shift.

00:30:58.289 --> 00:31:00.780
It's begun.

00:31:00.859 --> 00:31:02.656
What are you talking about?

00:31:02.727 --> 00:31:05.059
He's dying.

00:31:05.129 --> 00:31:08.098
Typically, I'm the one to make
that kind of prognosis.

00:31:08.166 --> 00:31:09.690
It's the nehret.

00:31:09.767 --> 00:31:10.699
It kills all of us

00:31:10.768 --> 00:31:12.827
who aren't fortunate
enough to die in battle.

00:31:19.077 --> 00:31:22.069
It's a retrovirus
that destroys the cells

00:31:22.146 --> 00:31:25.047
by attacking
the cytoplasmic membranes.

00:31:25.116 --> 00:31:26.811
Shouldn't our bio-filters
have detected it

00:31:26.885 --> 00:31:28.512
when we transported
the Klingons aboard?

00:31:28.586 --> 00:31:29.883
This is an insidious virus.

00:31:29.954 --> 00:31:31.581
It lies dormant,

00:31:31.656 --> 00:31:34.216
disguising itself
as inert genetic material

00:31:34.292 --> 00:31:36.658
until it inexplicably activates.

00:31:38.263 --> 00:31:40.390
The nehret always comes
without warning.

00:31:40.465 --> 00:31:42.865
I've reviewed my scans
of the other Klingons.

00:31:42.934 --> 00:31:44.561
They're all carriers.

00:31:47.138 --> 00:31:49.732
Why didn't you tell us
your people had a disease?

00:31:49.807 --> 00:31:52.503
We've never thought
of it as a disease.

00:31:52.577 --> 00:31:55.410
It's more like... old age.

00:31:55.480 --> 00:31:56.572
Is it contagious?

00:31:56.648 --> 00:31:59.014
Only to Klingons.

00:32:04.822 --> 00:32:06.687
If you'd give us some privacy,

00:32:06.758 --> 00:32:08.589
I'd like to examine
Lieutenant Torres.

00:32:08.660 --> 00:32:10.628
Of course.

00:32:29.981 --> 00:32:31.915
The baby, too?

00:32:31.983 --> 00:32:34.315
I'm afraid so.

00:32:38.523 --> 00:32:40.047
Why am I here?

00:32:42.126 --> 00:32:43.855
You're ill.

00:32:43.928 --> 00:32:45.259
You collapsed during the fight.

00:32:48.066 --> 00:32:49.431
The nehret.

00:32:49.500 --> 00:32:50.967
Yes.

00:32:51.069 --> 00:32:53.162
Thank you for telling us.

00:32:53.237 --> 00:32:55.671
Now my baby and I have it, too.

00:32:58.409 --> 00:33:00.400
Where do you think you're going?

00:33:00.478 --> 00:33:04.346
To prepare for my
journey to Sto-Vo-Kor.

00:33:04.415 --> 00:33:05.814
You should be in Sick Bay.

00:33:05.883 --> 00:33:07.851
Can you make me well?

00:33:07.919 --> 00:33:08.908
Not at the moment, but...

00:33:09.053 --> 00:33:11.385
Then don't deny
me my tradition.

00:33:29.340 --> 00:33:33.674
The child is not the kuvah'magh.

00:33:33.745 --> 00:33:36.043
But the father accepted
your challenge.

00:33:36.114 --> 00:33:37.046
He defeated you!

00:33:37.115 --> 00:33:40.607
I was defeated by the nehret!

00:33:42.020 --> 00:33:45.456
B'Elanna Torres and her child

00:33:45.523 --> 00:33:47.957
will fall victim to it as well.

00:33:48.092 --> 00:33:49.559
Impossible!

00:33:49.627 --> 00:33:51.822
They both carry it.

00:33:51.896 --> 00:33:53.386
She told me herself.

00:33:53.464 --> 00:33:55.329
But the Scrolls say

00:33:55.400 --> 00:33:57.868
the kuvah'magh
is younger than old age.

00:33:57.935 --> 00:34:02.201
And stronger than sickness.

00:34:02.273 --> 00:34:03.638
She cannot be our savior.

00:34:06.277 --> 00:34:08.745
We should resume our search.

00:34:08.813 --> 00:34:12.044
Kohlar and many
of the others won't agree.

00:34:12.116 --> 00:34:13.674
Then we must act alone!

00:34:15.953 --> 00:34:17.682
For the good of our people.

00:34:19.557 --> 00:34:21.047
How?

00:34:22.727 --> 00:34:25.924
We'll wait for
the right moment.

00:34:26.030 --> 00:34:28.396
And when it comes...

00:34:28.466 --> 00:34:30.661
we'll seize Voyager!

00:34:41.279 --> 00:34:43.804
We've identified
two potential colony sites

00:34:43.881 --> 00:34:45.508
in the southern hemisphere.

00:34:45.583 --> 00:34:47.881
We'll require
topographical scans.

00:34:47.952 --> 00:34:49.249
I'll prepare them.

00:34:52.657 --> 00:34:55.592
I shouldn't have doubted you.

00:34:55.660 --> 00:34:59.426
It appears the signs
were there all along.

00:34:59.497 --> 00:35:04.560
I'll join the survey mission.

00:35:04.635 --> 00:35:05.897
You're ill, old friend.

00:35:06.003 --> 00:35:07.903
You should remain here.

00:35:08.005 --> 00:35:13.602
I want my final days to be
spent in honorable pursuits.

00:35:13.678 --> 00:35:17.978
Don't ask me to die
inside these walls.

00:35:20.785 --> 00:35:22.753
We transport in one hour.

00:35:36.434 --> 00:35:39.699
Your transporters are much
more sophisticated than ours.

00:35:39.770 --> 00:35:41.704
I've studied Klingon
transport systems.

00:35:41.772 --> 00:35:44.138
The basic technology
isn't all that different.

00:35:44.208 --> 00:35:46.642
But you were able
to beam our entire crew

00:35:46.711 --> 00:35:48.235
aboard Voyager at one time.

00:35:48.312 --> 00:35:50.212
We usually don't like to do that

00:35:50.281 --> 00:35:52.272
for safety reasons,
but in a pinch,

00:35:52.350 --> 00:35:53.817
we can expand
the buffer capacity.

00:35:53.885 --> 00:35:55.352
These are the
targeting scanners?

00:35:55.419 --> 00:35:58.718
Exactly. They work on the
same principles as yours.

00:36:05.830 --> 00:36:07.092
You said it was urgent?

00:36:07.165 --> 00:36:08.257
I need to conduct

00:36:08.332 --> 00:36:10.266
a more detailed
bio-scan of your baby.

00:36:10.334 --> 00:36:11.596
She's not sick, is she?

00:36:11.669 --> 00:36:13.637
No, but I may be onto something.

00:36:15.640 --> 00:36:17.870
I'll be leading the team
going to Site A.

00:36:17.942 --> 00:36:20.877
Kohlar will be in charge
of the Site B team.

00:36:20.945 --> 00:36:22.037
Morning, Commander.

00:36:22.113 --> 00:36:23.102
Harry.

00:36:33.357 --> 00:36:36.292
Phaser fire
in Transporter Room 1.

00:36:36.360 --> 00:36:38.453
Bridge to Chakotay.

00:36:52.243 --> 00:36:54.074
They're on the surface.

00:36:54.145 --> 00:36:56.773
Now lock on to the
Bridge officers.

00:36:56.847 --> 00:36:59.941
They've activated a force field
around Deck 1.

00:37:00.017 --> 00:37:02.645
Transport the rest
of their crew.

00:37:02.720 --> 00:37:05.188
Captain, I'm detecting
multiple transports.

00:37:05.256 --> 00:37:08.555
Some of our people are being
beamed down to the surface.

00:37:08.626 --> 00:37:09.888
Cut power to the transporters.

00:37:12.096 --> 00:37:13.358
I can't.

00:37:13.431 --> 00:37:15.058
Bridge to Engineering.

00:37:16.100 --> 00:37:18.261
B'Elanna, respond.

00:37:18.336 --> 00:37:20.770
There's no one in Engineering.

00:37:25.576 --> 00:37:26.907
The Bridge officers?

00:37:27.011 --> 00:37:28.478
I still can't get a lock.

00:37:29.714 --> 00:37:32.182
Can you transport us there?

00:37:32.250 --> 00:37:33.842
I'll try.

00:37:41.726 --> 00:37:44.160
Computer, open
the Transporter Room doors.

00:37:44.228 --> 00:37:46.526
Security override:
Tuvok-pi-alpha.

00:38:27.605 --> 00:38:30.540
Grant me a warrior's death.

00:38:32.543 --> 00:38:34.204
I beg of you.

00:38:34.278 --> 00:38:35.540
Sorry.

00:38:35.613 --> 00:38:38.309
No mercy killings on my Bridge.

00:38:41.185 --> 00:38:42.652
Get our people back.

00:38:42.720 --> 00:38:45.245
Yes, ma'am.

00:39:01.272 --> 00:39:04.070
Why am I not in Sto-Vo-Kor?

00:39:04.141 --> 00:39:06.268
Because you are
healthy as a targ.

00:39:07.345 --> 00:39:09.472
The nehret?

00:39:09.547 --> 00:39:10.878
Gone.

00:39:11.015 --> 00:39:13.210
We have B'Elanna Torres' child

00:39:13.284 --> 00:39:15.013
to thank for it.

00:39:16.554 --> 00:39:18.385
The fetus has hybrid stem cells.

00:39:18.456 --> 00:39:20.424
They contain Klingon
and human DNA.

00:39:20.491 --> 00:39:22.686
I used them
to synthesize an antivirus.

00:39:22.760 --> 00:39:27.163
The child... cured me?

00:39:27.231 --> 00:39:28.789
Well, I was the one
who devised the treatment.

00:39:28.866 --> 00:39:29.890
Doctor...

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:32.833
Yes, of course,
the child cured you.

00:39:32.903 --> 00:39:34.530
The kuvah'magh

00:39:34.605 --> 00:39:37.039
has healed all of us.

00:39:37.108 --> 00:39:40.703
She truly is our savior.

00:39:49.387 --> 00:39:53.448
Captain's Log, Stardate 54529.8.

00:39:53.524 --> 00:39:56.049
While we're helping the Klingons
into their new home,

00:39:56.127 --> 00:39:59.153
life aboard Voyager is gradually
returning to normal.

00:40:01.899 --> 00:40:04.163
Computer, open this door.

00:40:04.235 --> 00:40:06.931
Access to these quarters
has been restricted.

00:40:07.071 --> 00:40:08.561
On whose authority?

00:40:08.639 --> 00:40:09.901
Neelix.

00:40:09.974 --> 00:40:12.534
Mr. Neelix, open this door.

00:40:12.610 --> 00:40:15.078
I'll be there in a minute,
Commander.

00:40:15.146 --> 00:40:16.636
That's... that's my boot.

00:40:16.714 --> 00:40:18.409
Computer, security override.

00:40:18.482 --> 00:40:19.779
Authorization: Tuvok-pi...

00:40:24.121 --> 00:40:26.419
Good-bye,
my little par'machkai.

00:40:26.490 --> 00:40:28.185
Good-bye, my fearless warrior.

00:40:28.259 --> 00:40:29.783
Oh!

00:40:41.172 --> 00:40:43.697
I'm really going to miss her.

00:40:55.453 --> 00:40:57.819
Oh...

00:41:00.858 --> 00:41:03.326
Don't you worry, Mr. Vulcan.

00:41:05.029 --> 00:41:07.930
I'll have this place...

00:41:08.032 --> 00:41:10.933
shipshape in no time at all.

00:41:12.970 --> 00:41:15.632
Just... go, Mr. Neelix.

00:41:24.148 --> 00:41:25.376
What's this?

00:41:25.449 --> 00:41:27.417
The bat'leth given to me

00:41:27.485 --> 00:41:28.952
by my great-grandfather.

00:41:29.019 --> 00:41:30.452
It's for your daughter.

00:41:32.223 --> 00:41:35.784
I hope someday
you'll tell her about us.

00:41:37.361 --> 00:41:39.261
I will.

00:41:49.440 --> 00:41:51.931
Qapla', B'Elanna Torres.

00:41:52.009 --> 00:41:54.477
Qapla'.

00:42:03.287 --> 00:42:04.584
It doesn't seem right

00:42:04.655 --> 00:42:06.350
just to hang it on the wall.

00:42:06.423 --> 00:42:09.358
I'm not letting you
scratch it up on the holodeck.

00:42:09.426 --> 00:42:11.053
I'm sure our daughter

00:42:11.128 --> 00:42:13.824
wouldn't mind lending it
to the old man

00:42:13.898 --> 00:42:15.229
every now and then.

00:42:15.299 --> 00:42:19.861
You know, this is one special
kid we're going to have.

00:42:19.937 --> 00:42:22.428
You're just figuring that out?

00:42:22.506 --> 00:42:25.270
Well, I was hoping
for an artist,

00:42:25.342 --> 00:42:27.071
or maybe a musician.

00:42:27.144 --> 00:42:32.138
But she's already the
savior of an entire race.

00:42:32.216 --> 00:42:34.343
You don't really believe that.

00:42:34.418 --> 00:42:35.680
I don't know.

00:42:35.753 --> 00:42:38.449
There are a lot
of coincidences to explain.

00:42:38.522 --> 00:42:39.580
I mean, what were the odds

00:42:39.657 --> 00:42:40.954
that they'd run
into the one ship

00:42:41.058 --> 00:42:42.889
in the whole Quadrant
with a Klingon aboard?

00:42:42.960 --> 00:42:44.757
Probably about the same odds

00:42:44.828 --> 00:42:46.955
that you and I
would get married.

00:42:48.365 --> 00:42:51.061
Maybe we should
name her kuvah'magh...

00:42:52.603 --> 00:42:54.127
Just to be safe.

00:42:57.808 --> 00:42:59.799
Put it on the list.
